  "rule": {
    "title": "Question tags with all tenses",
    "explanation": "Las question tags usan el auxiliar del verbo de la frase, en cualquier tiempo, y el pronombre del sujeto. Frase afirmativa → tag negativa, y al revés:\n- «will» → «won't»: «You'll come again, won't you?»\n- present perfect → «have» / «has»: «Daniel hasn't phoned yet, has he?»\n- past simple → «did»: «She made an apple tart, didn't she?»\n- «can», «should», «would»: «You can drive, can't you?», «We should go, shouldn't we?»\n- past continuous: «They were sleeping, weren't they?»\n\nCasos especiales:\n- «I am» → «aren't I?»: «I'm right, aren't I?»\n- «Let's» → «shall we?»: «Let's go to the cliffs, shall we?»\n- Imperativo → «will you?» / «won't you?»: «Have some more potatoes, won't you?»\n- Con «never», «nobody», «nothing», «hardly» (negativos), la tag va en afirmativa: «Nobody called, did they?», «It never stops raining, does it?»\n- «There is» → «isn't there?»: «There's a bus at six, isn't there?»",
    "table": {
